# Repo-wide line-ending policy. Text files are stored with LF and checked out with LF on every platform, so a Windows checkout
# (core.autocrlf=true, or an editor that saves CRLF) cannot commit CRLF into the repository. Before this line, 111 tracked files
# were committed as CRLF and every pre-commit run on Linux CI rewrote them (hook: mixed-line-ending --fix=lf).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts keep CRLF in the working tree: cmd.exe needs it, and the mixed-line-ending hook already excludes them.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Images and other binaries are never touched by the text filter.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.pdf binary
*.npy binary
*.npz binary
*.pkl binary

# Force LF regardless of checkout platform for files where CRLF breaks execution
# (a CRLF shebang line makes a script fail to run on Linux CI/dev boxes; shellcheck
# SC1017 catches this class of bug -- see scripts/run_numba_coverage.sh, 2026-07-06).
*.sh text eol=lf

# uv.lock is machine-generated and ~3 MB. Pin it to LF so a Windows checkout does not rewrite three
# megabytes of line endings into every diff, and mark it generated so review tooling collapses it --
# the reviewable part of a lock change is which versions moved, not the file body.
uv.lock text eol=lf linguist-generated=true
